{
  "hook": "plugin-validate",
  "_notes": [
    "plugin-validate has NO deny path — it is a PostToolUse context injector that always exits 0.",
    "Its three observable outcomes are: (1) silent exit 0, (2) a FAILED additionalContext block,",
    "(3) a warnings additionalContext block. The description string ('plugin.json',",
    "'marketplace.json', 'plugin (skill changed)', 'plugin (hooks changed)',",
    "'plugin (agents changed)', 'plugin (commands changed)') is embedded in the emitted context and",
    "is pinned per branch.",
    "Cases that must produce NON-EMPTY output use ABSOLUTE file paths, because `claude plugin",
    "validate` echoes the resolved absolute path of its target into stdout. The harness runs the",
    "python and the ts implementation in two DIFFERENT temp sandboxes, so any output containing the",
    "sandbox path would differ spuriously. Absolute targets outside the sandbox are identical for",
    "both runs. Fixture-based cases are therefore restricted to the branches whose output is empty."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "context-plugin-json-validation-failed",
      "kind": "context",
      "stdin": {
        "session_id": "sess-parity-pv-1",
        "hook_event_name": "PostToolUse",
        "tool_name": "Edit",
        "tool_input": {
          "file_path": "/nonexistent-parity/.claude-plugin/plugin.json"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "context-marketplace-json-validation-failed",
